+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Inventory and conflict foundation
+
+- [x] 1.1 Trace the existing product inventory, cart, checkout, order-status, and REST exception paths; document the concrete service/controller entry points in code comments or implementation notes and verify with targeted repository search.
+- [x] 1.2 Implement a shared stock validation and mutation path keyed by the exact product/SKU, including transactional decrement and restoration operations; verify with focused service tests that different products are never cross-decremented.
+- [x] 1.3 Add a stock-conflict business exception and map it to HTTP 409 for the affected REST endpoints; verify with controller/integration tests for the conflict response.
+
+## 2. Cart and checkout behavior
+
+- [x] 2.1 Enforce stock validation for new carts and single-item quantity changes, allowing reductions/removals and rejecting zero-stock additions or over-quantity updates without persistence; verify with cart API tests.
+- [x] 2.2 Make multi-item cart updates validate a prospective cart and persist all changes only after every line passes; verify a mixed valid/invalid request leaves the original cart unchanged.
+- [x] 2.3 Make both public and authenticated checkout paths validate all cart lines before creating an order, then decrement exactly the ordered products in one transaction; verify success, insufficient-stock atomic failure, and product-identity tests.
+
+## 3. Order cancellation and product availability
+
+- [x] 3.1 Restore stock on the first transition to CANCELED, make repeated cancellation a no-op, and reject all later status changes from CANCELED; verify status API tests for restoration, idempotence, conflict, and unchanged stock on other transitions.
+- [x] 3.2 Update product read availability and purchasability to combine merchant availability with positive stock; verify zero-stock, restocked, and merchant-disabled product API tests.
+- [x] 3.3 Run the relevant Maven module tests and the full stock regression suite, then fix any transaction or compatibility failures; verify with the recorded Maven command output.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the completed OpenSpec change after implementation and verification.
